Source: pg-living-assertions
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/Manuelreyesbravo/pg_living_assertions

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-living-assertions
Architecture: all
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Executable SQL assertions with recorded verification history
 pg_living_assertions stores SQL checks, their results, verification times
 and assertion replacement history. Checks run on demand in a read-only
 STABLE context. This is not a per-write SQL ASSERTION constraint.
 The distribution version is 0.4.2; the SQL extension version is 0.4.1.
